WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.234
-Sadie,
thank you for coming back.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.367
-Of course.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.367
-And thanks for being my partner
in charades.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:05.400
-Yeah, no, we killed it.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.667
-We crushed it, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.667
-Last time you were on the show,
we talked about --

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:11.033
I don't know if remember this --
you talked about playing Annie.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:12.701
-Yes.
-And I go --

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:15.901
We didn't have the video
to show, but now we do.

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:17.968
-Oh. It's my lucky day.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:21.534
-So here's 9-year-old Sadie Sink
as Annie performing "Tomorrow."

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:22.601
-[ Chuckling ] Oh.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:25.968
-♪ Tomorrow, tomorrow ♪

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.267
♪ I love ya ♪

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.801
♪ Tomorrow ♪

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:32.601
♪ You're always a day ♪

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:42.067
♪ Away ♪

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
-What?!

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.467
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:45.701
Get up! Come on, Sadie!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.100
Let's get out of here!

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.434
♪ Away ♪
Come on!

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:51.901
[ Cheers and applause continue ]
-Oh, my God. Thank you. Oh.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:52.901
-You've got some pipes there.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.634
-Oh.
-I mean, that's 9-years-old.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.100
-Had just turned 9, yeah.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.434
-And as
a very performing family?

00:00:58.434 --> 00:00:59.868
I just met your brother
backstage.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.400
-Yes.
-Is he musical, as well?

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.234
-Yes.
So, we did musical theater,

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:06.033
like, all throughout
our childhood,

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.167
and we'd, like,
put on musicals and everything.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.667
-Like, where?
Like, in the house?

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.667
-Yeah, like, in the house, we'd
do our own at-home production,

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.067
which is, like,
normal for theater kids.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.133
[ Audience cheers ]
What's not normal

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:19.667
is just continuing that behavior
at, like, an inappropriate age.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:22.968
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah.
Like, you've done it recently?

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:24.801
-Like, I'm very embarrassed,
but yes.

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:27.868
But to be fair,
it was during quarantine.

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:30.601
The movie "Cats"
had just come out.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.701
[ Laughter ]
We were all losing our minds,

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.834
and so naturally, like,
you know, we were like,

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:36.367
"Okay,
we have to do a home production

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.767
of 'Cats' the musical."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:41.033
But it was great.
It was high camp, lots of fun.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.834
-Yeah, and who was
the audience for this?

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:45.834
-Like, my parents
and my other two brothers,

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:48.234
and we FaceTimed
my grandparents in for it.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:49.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.033
I was probably 18 years old.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.667
Like, there's no excuse for it.
-No excuse for it.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.901
-I lost my mind.
-I love that -- at home.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.067
Why not? It's fantastic.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:56.667
Before we get to "The Whale"

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.133
and how great you were
in "The Whale,"

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.400
I haven't seen you since
"Stranger Things," Season 4,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.067
and man, oh, man,
you were just unbelievable.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.701
-Oh, thank you.
-It was fantastic.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:07.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.267
-Cliffhanger.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:12.467
-What do you hope for
for Max in Season 5?

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:15.100
-I mean, I would like to --
[ Sighs ]

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.534
I'd like to see her awake.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.434
-I want to know if I have to
get back in the body cast.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.367
I would like for that chapter
to be closed,

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:23.901
but, you know...
-Yeah, it didn't seem --

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.000
That's not the most fun part
of the show.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.067
-No.
-No.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:27.667
-But, honestly, you know,
just lie down.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.400
It's kind of an easy job.
-Yeah, I guess so.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.234
-But we'll see.
I have no clue.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.901
-And has the Kate Bush song
"Running Up That Hill"

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.701
gonna be like --
has that been your theme song

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.434
for the last year?
-It has.

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:39.167
-Yeah.
-Does it follow you around?

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:42.434
-It does.
I was in -- most recently,

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:45.100
I was in, like, Berlin,
in, like, a very tiny café.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.267
It was just me and my friend --
we're the only people there.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.434
And then, of course, like,
the song starts playing,

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:52.434
and everyone in the restaurant
is kind of like --

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:53.601
all the servers are like,

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:55.133
"Oh. What's she gonna do?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.801
-Like, "Is she gonna
start levitating?

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.367
What's happening?"
-No, like, that's my cue to go.

00:02:58.367 --> 00:02:59.734
-Yeah, it's like, "Yeah,
we got to get out of here."

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:02.834
Yeah.
I was in a club once --

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.634
this was back in the day
when I went to clubs.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.234
-Oh. Okay.
-Gosh. Whew!

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:08.200
Back -- "We used to have things
called clubs."

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:14.667
"Every young kid was there.
Oh, eh, oh."

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.968
But I went to this club,
and Axl Rose was there.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.200
And I love Axl Rose.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.267
And he was sitting there,
and they started playing

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:21.767
"Sweet Child o' Mine."

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.601
And he just stood up slowly,
and he goes...

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:25.767
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:27.067
He didn't want it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.167
-They should've turned it
right off.

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.267
-So that should be my move
next time.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:30.701
-That's your move.
You go -- Yeah.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.300
♪ Running up that hill ♪
-Stop.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.033
-No, no. No more, no.
-Cut it. No.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.701
-Let's talk about "The Whale."
-Yeah.

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.400
-Congrats.
You're getting rave reviews.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.667
You're nominated for
a Critics' Choice Award.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:41.901
Congratulations.
It's a big deal.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:43.501
-Thank you. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:45.767
[ Chuckles ]
-You are --

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.934
It's powerful. It is powerful.
It is powerful.

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:51.234
What a performance --
both of you guys.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:52.434
Did you know
that you were gonna get it

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:54.701
when you auditioned for this?

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.801
-Honestly, I thought
I kind of butchered it

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:59.334
because I had to do
the audition over Zoom

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.200
with Darren Aronofsky,
the director,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.701
and then Brendan Fraser,
who played my dad in it.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.834
And it was, like,
the final scene of the movie --

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:06.968
-No!
-If anyone's seen it --

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.601
it's, like,
a very, very intense scene.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:09.667
-That was the audition?

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.367
-Yes, that, and then
the first scene.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:14.367
But, like, to do it over Zoom,
kind of trying to, like...

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:15.434
-It's one
of the most emotional --

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.968
-...connect with each other --
It was --

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:18.634
So, I, like -- I hung up,
and I was like,

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.634
"Oh, I'm never going to see
these people again."

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:21.834
[ Laughter ]
"That's it."

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.167
-Yeah, you're like,
"Alright, come on, bro.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.167
Let's do 'Cats' one more time."
-Yeah, I know, yeah.

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:26.467
[ Laughter ]
Like, "Back to 'Cats.'"

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.767
-"It's getting a sequel.
'Cats' is getting a sequel."

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:31.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.968
But then -- well, you got it,
and you crushed it.

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.667
Have you been getting calls
and texts from everybody

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:36.667
saying how good you are?

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.567
-Yes, I have,
but I'm kind of going through,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:41.234
like, a --
like, a phone issue right now.

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:44.033
Because, like, my phone broke,
and I don't back it up,

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.300
and I don't really know
what the cloud is or anything.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.501
So I lost all my contacts.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.467
So people are sending
really sweet messages,

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:52.534
but I just don't know
who they are.

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:55.167
And sometimes I can use, like,
context clues

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:56.734
and piece things together.

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:58.300
-Like, what do you mean?
Like, somebody will...

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.367
-Like, Noah Schnapp,
for example --

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:01.868
he texted me the other day.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.767
-And he always, like,
sends my name first,

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.133
just like, "Sadie."

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.067
And I was like, "Oh, okay."
-That's Noah.

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.200
-That's Noah.
-Alright, so you're like,

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.200
"Thank you, Noah.
I appreciate it.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.434
You're awesome.
What's up, bud?"

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.834
-But everyone else,
I have no clue,

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:13.000
so I've just been giving --
-They're like, "Great job."

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.501
And you're like...
-"Thank you!"

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:18.467
And just trying to gather, like,
context clues as you go along.

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:19.634
-So, if anyone's gotten
like a --

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.634
kind of a dud of a response
from Sadie --

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.167
-Yeah, honestly, like,
I'm really glad

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:25.100
that we're talking about this
'cause it's been horrible.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.033
And if any of my friends
are watching it, like,

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.901
just send your name
with a text message.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:30.234
-Just send your name, saying,

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:31.400
"Sadie, checking in again,
this is my name."

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.100
-I'm sorry. Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, and we're good.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.000
Can we set up what "The Whale"
is about for everyone?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.767
-Yeah, so, "The Whale"
is about a man named Charlie

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:42.734
who is a reclusive
English teacher.

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:45.100
And he lost the love
of his life.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.534
And ever since he died,

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:50.767
he kind of has been spiraling
into this deep depression,

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:53.133
has been self-medicating
with food.

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.501
And the movie
is kind of set during

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.200
what is likely
the last week of his life.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:00.100
So he attempts to reconnect
with his daughter,

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.000
who he had left when
she was around 10 years old.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.767
-Well done.
-And that is the movie.

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:04.968
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.100
-That was a great job.
I want to show a clip.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.567
Here's Sadie Sink
in "The Whale."

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.133
Look at this.

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:14.167
-You don't have to be angry
at the whole world.

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:17.000
[ Grunts ]

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.300
You can just be angry at me.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.834
-Okay.
You know what?

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:23.133
You can't throw me away
like I'm a piece of garbage

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:26.400
and then suddenly just want to
be my dad eight years later!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.601
You left me for your boyfriend.
-[ Sighs ]

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.334
It's that simple.

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:32.934
And if you've been telling
yourself anything different,

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:34.868
then you're lying to yourself.

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:39.334
But you know what?
I'm glad.

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:40.634
I'm -- I'm glad

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:43.701
because you taught me
something very important --

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:47.567
people are [bleep].

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:50.334
Most people learn that
way too late.

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:52.767
You -- You taught me that
when I was 8.

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:57.100
Thank you for that.
[ Sniffles ]

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.400
-Oh, my gosh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.300
Well done.
-Thank you.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.968
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:07.868
-Sadie, you're an actor
and part of your craft

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:10.200
is making all kinds of sounds

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.934
and, you know, for the things...

00:07:11.934 --> 00:07:13.000
-Sure.
-...so I thought it'd be fun

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.701
for us to make some sounds
right now.

00:07:14.701 --> 00:07:16.234
It is time
for the Mimic Challenge.

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:17.534
Here we go.

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.734
[ Cheering and applause ]
-♪ Mimic Challenge ♪

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:20.834
♪ Mimic, mimic ♪

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:24.033
♪ Challenge, yeah ♪

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:25.601
-Now, how it works is we're
going to take turns

00:07:25.601 --> 00:07:27.467
making noises
with different objects, okay?

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:29.167
And the other person has
to immediately match

00:07:29.167 --> 00:07:31.234
that sound
as precisely as they can.

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:33.067
Sound okay? Don't look.
Are you ready?

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:34.934
I will make
the first noise for you.

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:36.133
Here we go. Ready?
-Oh.

00:07:36.133 --> 00:07:37.167
-Okay.

00:07:37.167 --> 00:07:39.601
Sadie, make --
make this sound.

00:07:39.601 --> 00:07:40.934
I don't know if I can do this.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:41.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.267
-Can I do this?

00:07:43.267 --> 00:07:45.000
Pbbbbbbbt!

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.501
-Khhhhhhh!

00:07:51.501 --> 00:07:52.834
[ Laughter ]
-Wow! That's not bad.

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:54.067
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Ding ]

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:55.100
[ Rimshot ]
That's pretty good.
-Yeah.

00:07:56.601 --> 00:07:58.200
-Alright, now,
this is my turn to mimic.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.200
-Okay.
-This is this.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.534
-Oh.
Alright, Jimmy.

00:08:02.534 --> 00:08:04.200
-Mm-hmm.
-Make this sound

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.834
[ Mooing ]

00:08:05.834 --> 00:08:07.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.901 --> 00:08:09.234
One more time?
-It's a lot longer
than you'd think.

00:08:09.234 --> 00:08:10.467
[ Mooing ]

00:08:10.467 --> 00:08:12.467
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.467 --> 00:08:14.200
Hurrrrrrrrrrrrr!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:08:15.267 --> 00:08:16.734
That's like on pitch.

00:08:16.734 --> 00:08:18.200
[ Rimshot ]
-Not bad. On pitch?
-Yeah.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:18.968
Look at you.

00:08:18.968 --> 00:08:20.801
-Alright.
[ Chuckles ]

00:08:20.801 --> 00:08:23.734
Sadie...
-Oh. No. [ Laughs ]

00:08:23.734 --> 00:08:24.667
Make this sound.

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:26.067
[ Chipmunk squeaking ]

00:08:26.067 --> 00:08:28.834
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:31.501
-Whah whah whah whah whah whah
whah whah whah whah.

00:08:31.501 --> 00:08:32.634
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]
It's kind of --

00:08:32.634 --> 00:08:34.133
You know, it sounds like a cat.

00:08:34.133 --> 00:08:35.300
I was ready for that.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.367
-Oh? Good, yeah.
-Yeah, mm-hmm.

00:08:36.367 --> 00:08:38.467
-That was perfect
and also on pitch.

00:08:38.467 --> 00:08:39.968
Alright, this one.

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:40.901
Alright, let me see
if I can get this one.

00:08:40.901 --> 00:08:42.000
-Oh.
-Oh.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.133
-Hm.

00:08:43.133 --> 00:08:44.467
Okay.
[ Honk ]

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:45.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:45.434 --> 00:08:46.701
-Okay.
[ Honk honk ]

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:47.634
Alright.

00:08:47.634 --> 00:08:49.467
Give it to me one more time.

00:08:49.467 --> 00:08:51.067
[ Honk ]
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.067 --> 00:08:51.834
[ Braying ]
Huahhh!

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:53.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:54.667
[ Rimshot ]
-Yes! Yes.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:55.767
[ Ding ]
-[ Brays ] Huahh! It's, like,

00:08:55.767 --> 00:08:57.501
a little breathy.
-Hunnh! That was great.

00:08:57.501 --> 00:08:59.200
-It was a little breathy.
-Okay.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.334
-Alright. Alright.
How about this?

00:09:01.334 --> 00:09:05.534
This is a text message.
-Oh.

00:09:05.534 --> 00:09:07.000
[ Cellphone bloops ]

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.000
-Oooh-errr!
Oooh-errr!

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.567
-[ Laughs ]
[ Ding ]

00:09:11.567 --> 00:09:12.901
-Oooh-errr!

00:09:12.901 --> 00:09:16.434
-Alright. Is this -- This is --
-Oh. I have -- Okay.

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:19.400
-Spreading butter on toast?
-Oh. Alright, Jimmy.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.534
Make this sound.

00:09:21.534 --> 00:09:23.901
Maybe it will catch -- Yeah.

00:09:23.901 --> 00:09:25.634
[ Butter knife scraping ]

00:09:25.634 --> 00:09:27.334
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:29.567 --> 00:09:31.334
[ Scraping echoes ]
-No, I'm sorry.

00:09:31.334 --> 00:09:32.334
-That's cheating.
-I'm sorry. No, no, no.

00:09:32.334 --> 00:09:33.434
You can't do that.
You want more?

00:09:33.434 --> 00:09:34.901
-Yeah, I want to hear it.
-You want more?

00:09:34.901 --> 00:09:37.167
[ Butter knife scraping ]

00:09:37.167 --> 00:09:40.567
-Khhrrrr! Khhrrrr! Khhrrrr!
-Oh. Oh, yes.

00:09:40.567 --> 00:09:41.734
[ Ding ]
Yes.

00:09:41.734 --> 00:09:42.968
[ Applause ]
-Was is it too --

00:09:42.968 --> 00:09:44.200
-Very nice.
-Was it so realistic?

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.834
-It was so good.
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:45.834 --> 00:09:47.367
-Whoa! Whoa!
-Oh, my gosh.

00:09:47.367 --> 00:09:48.434
I am so embarrassed.

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:49.501
Okay.
-Great. Two minutes.

00:09:49.501 --> 00:09:50.801
This is the --
-Take the toast.

00:09:50.801 --> 00:09:52.067
-Thank you very much.
Yes, I got the toast.

00:09:52.067 --> 00:09:53.534
This is the last round here.

00:09:53.534 --> 00:09:56.501
This one is for you.
Here we go.

00:09:56.501 --> 00:09:59.868
[ Netflix tone plays ]

00:09:59.868 --> 00:10:02.767
-♪ Da-dunnnn ♪
-♪ Whaaaaa ♪

00:10:02.767 --> 00:10:04.100
[ Ding ]
-That's it right there!

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.667
That's how the pros do it!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:05.667 --> 00:10:07.133
Sadie Sink!

00:10:07.133 --> 00:10:09.534
[ Cheers and applause continue ]
"The Whale" is in theaters now.

00:10:09.534 --> 00:10:11.734
We'll be right back
with a performance from Dayglow.

00:10:11.734 --> 00:10:12.801
Stick around.
[ Cheers and applause ]

